---
title: Dreamy Cheese Cake
author: Judy White
category: Desserts
cook time: 10 minutes
source: Loving Memories of Mildred
---

@flour{1%cup}
@melted butter{1%cube}
@brown sugar{0.25%cup}
@cream cheese{1%8-oz package}
@sugar{1%cup}
@lemon Jell-O{1%small package} (dissolved in 1 cup hot water)
@prepared Dream Whip{1%small package}
@lemon Jell-O{1%large package} (or 2 small packages, dissolved in 3 cups of hot water)

==Crust==
Mix flour, melted butter, and brown sugar and press down into greased 9x13 pan. Bake at 375 degrees for 10 minutes.

==Filling==
Cream the sugar and cream cheese, pour in the cooled Jell-O and mix. Mix in whipped cream until smooth and pour mixture on cold crust. Refrigerate until stiff.

==Topping==
Set dissolved Jell-O until cool and pour over the stiff mixture. Refrigerate. (Any flavor Jell-O can be substituted for the lemon)
